  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a hotel conversion in **North America** where **affiliation flexibility** is the priority, owners should look first at the major **soft-brand / collection** options from the big chains, plus independent-affiliation platforms that preserve more operating freedom.[2][7][9][16]\n\nThe most commonly cited choices are:\n\n- **Marriott**: **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, and **Luxury Collection** are the best-known soft/collection options for independent or conversion-minded hotels.[12][15][16]\n- **Hilton**: **Curio Collection by Hilton** and **Tapestry Collection by Hilton** are the core Hilton soft-brand conversion pathways.[5][12][18]\n- **Choice Hotels**: **Ascend Hotel Collection** is a major soft-brand option, especially for independents seeking chain distribution with lighter brand standards.[15][16]\n- **Best Western**: **Best Western Premier Collection** is another soft-brand route used by independent hotels.[15]\n- **Wyndham**: **Trademark Collection**, **Registry Collection Hotels**, and **Dolce Hotels and Resorts** are specifically presented by Wyndham as soft-brand options for one-of-a-kind properties.[2]\n- **IHG**: **Vignette Collection** and **voco hotels** are IHG’s soft-brand choices; **Garner hotels** is also explicitly described as conversion-friendly and flexible, though it is positioned more as a conversion brand than a classic soft brand.[11]\n- **Hyatt**: **Unbound Collection by Hyatt** is a notable collection brand for distinctive, conversion-suitable hotels.[12]\n- **Preferred Hotels & Resorts** and **The Leading Hotels of the World**: these are not franchise soft brands in the strict chain sense, but they are often considered by owners who want affiliation with high autonomy and less rigid brand control.[16][18]\n\nIf the owner’s main goal is the **greatest flexibility in design, operations, and brand identity**, the most relevant short list is usually **Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Curio Collection, Tapestry Collection, Ascend Hotel Collection, and Preferred/LHW-style affiliation networks**.[7][9][16][18]\n\nA practical way to think about it is:\n\n- **Most chain support + still flexible**: Marriott, Hilton, IHG, Wyndham soft brands.[2][11][12]\n- **More independence, less prescribed brand control**: Preferred Hotels & Resorts, Leading Hotels of the World.[16][18]\n- **Especially conversion-friendly / lower-friction options**: IHG’s Garner, and flexible midscale collection concepts where available.[1][11]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **ranked shortlist for a specific asset type** like upscale urban, resort, boutique, or midscale conversion.",
